        <p>St. John's Presbyterian—Morning and even- ing, Rev. W. Reid. Legh-street Primitive Methodist—Morning Mr. A. Metcalfe: evening, Rev. A. J. chessuna: Canal Mystery Solved. On Tuesday morning the body of an unknown man was recovered from the Manchester Ship Canal at Walton, and later in the day Deputy _Coroner F. A. Jones held an inquest at the Warrington Coroner's Court. The man was about 40 years of age, and sft. 2in. in height. lie had probably been in the water six weeks or two months. Four shillings and sixpence were found in his possession, but there was nothing whatever to lead to identification. No- body was reported missing from this district, and it was surmised that the body was that of a foreign seaman, which had been carried up the canal. The body was identified on Thurs- day as that of Charles Lee, storekeeper, from the as. Algeriern, and who resided at 32, Shir- ley-street, Canning Town, London. The wife , of deceased proved identification, and Lee was buried at the Cemetery. -</p>
