        <p>Bachelors Entertain. On New Year's night the members of the Young Men's Bible Class associated with the Working Men's Mission* entertained a com- pany of 140 guests to tea. The concert, which was presided over by Mr. A. Dennett, was pro- vided by the bachelor element. A pianororte solo was well rendered by Mr. A. Allinson, as also was a clarioi4ette solo by Mr. L. Gough. Master F. Dowling added to his reputation by 11 two humorous recitations, while as a society 'entertainer, Mr. G. B. Starkie proved his capa- bilities in "The Village Bazaar." and A Clean Sweep." Competitions for ladies and gentle- men were entered into with zest.</p>
