        <p>Locomotives Nearing the North Pole. Slowly the locomotive follows the explorers toward the North Pole, just as it did to the heart of Africa and over the Andes; across the plains of the \Vest and the steppes of the East. NoW it is Iceland that is to have a railroad, the closest one yet to the Arctic Circle, and that frozen little isle's first line of track. The new improvement will consist of about six and one- quarter miles of track around the city of ileyk- lavik and its harbour, and the improvement I will not be completed before 1916.</p>
