      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-01-03_WidnesExaminer_art0167" n="art0167">
        <head>CHILDREN'S BALL.</head>
        <p>CHILDREN'S BALL.</p>
        <p>Another Suceessful Effort for the Children's Cot.</p>
        <p>AN IMPRESSIVE SIGHT.</p>
        <p>"VICTORY OR DEATH " AT THE PARK PALACE.</p>
        <p>The scene of a vessel on fire whilst out at sea and a young woman bound and imprisoned in I one of the cabins provides an exciting episode in the film "Victory or Death," which occupies the principal position at the Park Picture Palace for the latter part of this week. The film was in three parts and was crowded with exciting incidents. The "Rival Musicians" wa3.n comedy film with a pleasing plot, whilst ' for originality of plot. "Pimple s Inferno" will require much effort to excel,- The film ".Cinderella's Slipper" has an enjoyable tale to unfold, and, with other pictures, a good pro- gramme is submitted. , Next Week's " Park" Programme. , An unusually good programme is to be sub- mitted at the Park Picture Palace next week, when, for Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday, the principal film will be "The Key," a picture of misunderstanding, which will be supplemented by other pictures, including the drama "Miss Arabian Night," and several containing a strong sense of humour. For the latter part of the week the "star" picture will be an excellent seasonable film. entitled "The Newsboy's Christmas Dream." A striking feature will be provided by "A Child of the Sea," a picture of natural beauty, in two Farts' and bt-r6 " Willie at Blackpool" will be cc n.</p>
      </div>
