        <p>THE EXAMINER, SATURDAY, JANUARY 3, 1914.</p>
        <p>THE PICTUREDROME. Evidence of the popularity of the Picture- drome is given by the attendance at every house. The present week's • programme has been of a very interesting character. On Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday principal in- terest centred round the film "The Comedian's Mask," whilst since Wednesday a drama in three parts, entitled "For Ever," has taken its place. The programme also includes comedy, scenic and educational subjects. NEXT WEEK. "The Old Melody," a tale of how a melody arises out of the past and re-unites husband and wife, will be shown from Monday to Wednes- day, and for the remainder of the week "The Stolen Formula" will occupy the chief place.</p>
