        <p>PRIME MINISTER'S INSPIRING MESSAGE. How the New Year Finds the Liberal Party. • NEVER IN BETTER HEALTH AND SPIRITS. The Prime Minister has sent the followinginspi message to " The Liberal Monthly 10, Downing-street, Whitehall, S.W. "I gladly send you a message to the readers of ' The Liberal Monthly,' to appear in the first issue for 1914. and never within my experience has the " It is now eight years since we came into Power, Liberal Party been in better health and spirits. " We have placed on the Statute Book measures of constitutional and social reform of the first importance; other measures not less important are nearing their goal; and we are setting on foot, with the unswerving support of a united party, an organised campaign against the abuses connected with the present system of land "We believe that what we have done and what tanimates tenure. we and guides us, I feel confident are doing is in accord with the best less glorious than the past. traditions of Libeyalism, and so long as that sP r that Liberals may look forward to a future no " Yours very faithfully, December 18th, 1913.</p>
