        <p>FROST VETOES NEW YEAR'S DAY FOOTBALL. Owing to the severe frost during the week the New Year's Hay football programme was Aliattered locally:. The final in the Lancashire Junior Cup was down for decision for eleven o'clock in the morning between. Rylands' Recs. and Abram Rangers, but this, together with the Warrington "A" v. Runcorn "A" Combination match had to be abandoned. 'rhe Warrington senior team were to have ful- filled the usual League fixture at Runcorn, but a telephone message on Thursday morning from that club announced that football was out. of the question, owing to the hard state of the ground. • • The Arrangements. The postponed Lancashire Junior Cup final may take place next Saturday. We have no official communication in the matter, but we understand that the "A" team match with Wigan Highfield, originally agreed for that day, has been re-arranged, and that a friendly match with Sutton has been fixed up. That might very easily be abandoned or postponed, if con- venient to the Clubs concerned in the final. Councillor Osborne to Present the Cup. Councillor Osborne. chairman of the War- rington Yootball CommitWe, and the club's representative on the Northern Rugby Football Union and the Lancashire County Football Union, has been invited to present the cup and medals to the winning team in the Lancashire Junior Cup final.</p>
