        <p>NEW PICTURE PALACE. For the first three days of the week an excep- tionally fine film entitled "Secret of the Ring" was the principal "draw." How rubber is packed for exportation is seen in a picture descriptive of a tramp through manoes. The latter part of the week has mostly been occu- pied by the film, "Where is Colletti?" • NEXT WEEK. The ever-popular "Beauty and the Beast" is to be presented by the aid of a film at the New Picture House next Thursday, Friday and Saturday, and should prove an exceptional draw, for it is a magnificent spectacular pan- tomime. A picture full of marvellous and real- istic situations, entitled "Victory or Death," will arouse chief interest for the earlier part of the week. The other films are of merit.</p>
