        <p>LATE DISTRICT NEWS: GRAPPEN HALL: , Tea Party.—Suecess waited upon the annual - party of the Grappenhall Independent Metho- dists on Thursday evening, when, following an excellent tea, a pleasing programme was sub- 'mitted by the following: Misses Harmer and Peacock and Messrs. Knowles, Gough and Jones (songs), and Mr. Wilkes, Master Harold Henshall, and Miss Blanche Lewis (recitations). Councillor Henshall presided, and gave an in:- teresting address. There was a large attend- ance.—The festivities were continued last even- ing, when the Sunday school children gathered for their party and prize distribution. ' PENH ETH• . Wesleyan Church: Watchnight Annual Social and Service.—This took place at the Wesleyan S.chools on New Year's Eve. The Rev. H. Middlewood presided. The musical programme included the band quartet, sketeh, 'll,ly wife's _relatives," rendered by members of the We-sic:yen Church, which was specialty appreciated by a large company. Mr. Tinley (secretary of the Wesley Guild) is to be con- gratulated on being able to get the Latchford friends to assist. Songs were suitably given hy local artistes in good style. After refreshments had been served, games were indulged in and enjoyed, as of yore. The members and. friettds about 11 p.m.•,transferred themselves to the chapel. where the service was held. The Rev. H. Middlewood occupied the pulpit. After the stroke of 12 (midnight) hearty handshakes and good wishes were given at the dawn of the New- Year. The arrangements, as usual, were car- ried out by Mr. Parker's Men's Bible. Class and the Guild Committee. Death of Mn. Martha Broom.—We regret to record the death of an old inhabitant of Pen- /ieth in the person of Mrs. Martha Broom, wife of Mr. W. Broom, of Chapel-road. The deceased, who had periodically suffered a great deal, passed away rather suddenly on Tueaday night. She was a member of St. Mary's Church and also of the Women's Guild. Mr. Broom anti family have the sympathy of a large number of friends in their sorrow. The funeral takes place to-day (Saturday).</p>
